diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 550aa94..dc8f2ff 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@ All pull requests merged to `main`, in reverse chronological order.
 
 - **ChatGPT plan usage**: An optional extension estimates the API value of ChatGPT plan usage for the ChatGPT plan and Codex CLI providers. It tracks tokens used in AESPA and reads the plan's 5-hour and weekly usage percentages from the Codex CLI, including when a scan using either provider starts and ends. Readings where the percentage changed while AESPA used no tokens are left out. Stats → ChatGPT Plan Usage shows usage over time, estimated cost, and tokens per percentage point. Reading intervals are configurable. Usage outside AESPA affects the estimates; prices come from the Usage page.
 
-- **Crawler workflows**: After the page crawl, AESPA tries to reach useful workflows it missed. Up to three workflows run at the same time, each in its own browser session with its own sign-in, so they don't share cookies or application state. When a workflow needs test data, a **Needs input** button appears at the top of the run on every tab. It opens a side panel where you can supply the data without leaving the tab you're on, and save successful instructions for later crawls. You can continue several workflows at once. Needs input names the field or option the crawler needs. To choose an option such as a payment method, name it as it appears on the page, for example "Pay by bank transfer". Reached workflows become checks in the Test Lead's coverage work and appear in the Workflows view of OWASP Coverage, laid out like the page table. The Pages and Workflows switch sits at the top of OWASP Coverage, and the Progress summary shows only on Pages because it counts page checks. Each workflow is checked for skipped or reordered steps. Depending on what it does, it can also be checked for access by another account, repeated or simultaneous submission, changed amounts or prices, cross-site request forgery, and sensitive changes made without signing in again. Full scans require each check to be tested or marked blocked with a reason.
+- **Crawler workflows**: After the page crawl, AESPA tries to reach useful workflows it missed. Up to three workflows run at the same time, each in its own browser session with its own sign-in, so they don't share cookies or application state. When a workflow needs test data, a **Needs input** button appears at the top of the run on every tab. It opens a side panel where you can supply the data without leaving the tab you're on, and save successful instructions for later crawls. You can continue several workflows at once. Needs input names the field or option the crawler needs. To choose an option such as a payment method, name it as it appears on the page, for example "Pay by bank transfer". All identified workflows appear in OWASP Coverage, including ones the crawler could not reach. Crawl progress has its own column. Reached functions get separate security checks; workflows awaiting a crawl show no completed checks. Workflows reached during the normal page crawl are included, and they do not raise a Needs input notice. The Pages and Workflows switch sits at the top of OWASP Coverage, and the Progress summary shows only on Pages because it counts page checks. Each workflow is checked for skipped or reordered steps. Depending on what it does, it can also be checked for access by another account, repeated or simultaneous submission, changed amounts or prices, cross-site request forgery, and sensitive changes made without signing in again. Full scans require each check to be tested or marked blocked with a reason.
 
 - **Grouped page crawl**: The optional **Group similar pages** setting samples pages with similar layouts, such as products or articles, and groups them on the site map. This leaves more of the crawl budget for distinct site features. Sampling limits indexing only. The Test Lead can test other in-scope pages and records for access control, ownership, and other security checks without indexing the whole group. Results apply to the requests and records tested. The setting is off by default.
 
